<title>NORWAY: Fokus share jumps on takeover bid.</title>
<headline>Fokus share jumps on takeover bid.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Fokus Bank, Norway's third largest commercial bank, rose sharply on Monday following a takeover bid by Sparebankgruppen, a group of 16 savings banks.</p>
<p>The share was up seven crowns, about 10 percent, at 75.50 crowns in heavy turnover of 216 million crowns after 45 minutes of trade on the Oslo Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Sparebankgruppen said it was bidding 73 crowns per share for Fokus, which is valued at 4.80 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Rolf Soderlind, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
